rsing four columns in every instance I've examined so far.\n\n**Defining Single-Digit Rules**\n\nI'm solidifying the rules for single digits. Specifically, '1' appears to remain stationary, add two '5's to its right, and then a '1' moves diagonally up-right by two columns, while '2' moves left by four columns, filling between with '5's.\n\n**Refining Intersection Logic**\n\nI'm diligently refining how rule applications interact. It appears the '2' moving left introduces '5's that can conflict with other rules, like the '6' moving up. I'm currently testing a hypothesis where the '2's movement might be truncated or altered by such intersections.\n\n**Investigating Intersection Dynamics**\n\nI'm now focusing on how the '2' moving left interacts with other elements, particularly the '6' moving up. It appears this intersection point consistently generates a diagonal of '4's extending down-left. I'm analyzing the exact trajectory and termination conditions of this diagonal.\n\n",
